      At line 302: regs->epc += get_break_insn_length(regs->epc) modifies the saved epc through the struct pt_regs pointer. This is the breakpoint/BUG trap path. The advance is conditional (only for BUG_TRAP_TYPE_WARN or CFI failure), but when it fires, it writes directly to offset 0 of the pt_regs. If CLIC pushpop placed a status CSR at offset 0, this would corrupt privileged state. Also notable: line 300-301 read regs->epc for instruction decoding and line 302 writes back to it — a TOCTOU-like write to the same field, though not an actual TOCTOU since it's the same sequence (read, decode, advance).
